nss_hal: ipq50xx: deassert ALL UBI0 reset lines, not just bits 0-2

The GCC register at 0x1868010 (nss-misc-reset) carries six reset lines on
IPQ5018 (mainline gcc-ipq5018.c): AXI(0), AHB(1), NC_AXI(2), DBG(3),
UTCM(6) and CORE(7). The QSDK HAL clears only bits 0-2 (mask 0x7) and
relies on the remaining bits being deasserted by the boot chain - which
holds on the downstream 5.4 kernel but not on mainline, leaving the UBI32
core in reset: clocks spin, firmware is copied, but the core never
executes (no SOS, no h2n consumption, phys_if timeouts).

Clear all six lines. For lines already deasserted this is a no-op.

Verified on GL-B3000 (IPQ5018, fw 12.2-156 and 12.5-210): with mask 0x7
the core never boots; with 0xcf it reports "nss core 0 booted
successfully" and sustains ~890 Mbit/s of accelerated forwarding.

--- a/nss_hal/ipq50xx/nss_hal_pvt.c
+++ b/nss_hal/ipq50xx/nss_hal_pvt.c
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
 /*
  * Core GCC reset
  */
-#define NSS_CORE_GCC_RESET 0x00000007
+#define NSS_CORE_GCC_RESET 0x000000cf
 
 /*
  * GCC reset
